  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 129 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe upper level high will remain east of the area with an upper \nlevel trough over the western United States throughout the forecast. \nThis will place southwest flow above western Kansas. High pressure \nwill be the dominate feature at the surface with a trough of low \npressure moving closer to western Kansas this weekend into the first \npart of next week as an upper level low moves through the \nIntermountain West. Dry conditions are expected throughout the \nforecast, but a few stray thunderstorms may be possible during peak \nheating this weekend into the early part of next week. Winds will \ngenerally be from a southerly direction through at least the early \npart of next week with no frontal passages expected. Very hot \nconditions are expected over the next 7 days with highs reaching \ninto the upper 90s to low 100s with lows ranging from the mid 60s to \nmid 70s.",
